daenerys targaryen played by emilia  clarke quickly became one of the most  popular characters in game of thrones  audiences hopped on board her hellbent  mission to bring her rage to westeros  and oust the lannisters from the seat of  power the iron throne which daenerys  believes is her birthright the show  spends plenty of time developing her  character in a way that made audiences  feel incredibly sympathetic towards her  cause she's undoubtedly one of the  show's most beloved heroes  i need to be more than that once she  fully came into her own commanding  armies and fighting for justice daenerys  was indisputably a brilliant and  compelling character not to mention the  addition of her dragons which only made  fans invest in her quest even further  while it was obvious what producers d.b  weiss and david benioff were trying to  say about the allure that true power  holds and how it easily corrupts people  one particular scene took things too far  this is of course when daenerys burned  king's landing it's a moment that  unfortunately turned fans against  daenerys in the final season of game of  thrones okay sure daenerys burned people  alive using her dragons a number of  times but it's the intention behind the  destruction of king's landing that just  took things too far now we can admit  that daenerys was in a bad place jon  snow played by kit harington rejected  her because he discovers they're related  yikes she loses both her closest  confidant missandei played by natalie  emmanuel and one of her two remaining  dragons to cersei's forces daenerys has  nothing left to lose which leads to the  complete destruction of king's landing  in season 8 episode 5 the bells it's  completely daenerys choice to willingly  burn probably thousands of innocent  people including women and children  alive in the streets the civilians  collective terror is truly felt  throughout the episode with a war  happening on the ground and a  fire-breathing dragon hovering in the  sky at this point daenerys is no longer  a liberator it's a complete departure  from and portrayal of the woman who was  so dedicated to freeing slaves for the  past seven seasons when faced with  king's landing daenerys kills thousands  of people simply because she can as the  battle rages jon is horrified by her  actions when he sees the burned bodies  of men women and children litter the  ground it's only further hammered home  that dany is truly off the deep end when  she announces in the season finale the  iron throne that she was planning to  extend her wrath across the rest of the  world jon ultimately faces an impossible  choice and kills his queen aunt and  lover right in front of the throne she  wants so badly there's no question that  daenerys a hot-blooded targaryen with a  family history of mental instability and  massive dragons willing to do her  bidding made some troubling decisions  throughout thrones still viewers could  always be comforted that she was on the  right side of justice that is until the  show's final season the creative minds  behind game of thrones maintained that  the daenerys twist was planned all along  and it makes sense with her character  however the daenerys that audiences fell  for would never have killed innocents  though clark initially defended the  finale back in may of 2019 saying  daenerys destruction was a logical route  for the character to take she has since  reversed course during a june 2021 chat  with mtv news correspondent josh  horowitz on his podcast clark said i get  why people were pissed i totally get it  though clark said she did have some  quote autonomy over daenerys character  arc when all was said and done she just  had to play what was given to her as  truthfully as possible she added the  editor decides what it looks like and  the writer decides what i'm saying so  you just gotta go in and try and give it  as much truth and honesty and yourself  as you possibly can whether you want to  relive daenerys's 